description:
Define and enforce the readiness gate that separates migration audits from the first citable four-layer baseline.

A migration report may show legacy or unscorable records so work can be tracked. Baseline series 1 may not freeze until:

- every accepted record validates against the canonical contract version;
- no accepted record reaches evaluation through a legacy key, loader exemption, source-token-only identity, or unadjudicated flow endpoint;
- legacy flow and data-item records have been accepted canonically, rejected, or moved to `needs_adjudication`;
- each headline layer meets an explicitly approved minimum accepted-case and packet-diversity threshold;
- packet-and-layer precision scopes carry review provenance;
- path-contract errors and unscorable rates meet explicit limits;
- all required materializations and source SHAs validate;
- the readiness result is emitted as machine-readable evidence and rendered in the baseline report.

Data flows reported as unscorable pending regold belong to a readiness audit, not baseline series 1. A small canonical subset may be used only if its size/diversity threshold is declared and approved; silently dropping 436 legacy flow records is forbidden.

Definition of done: the baseline command refuses to freeze when any readiness invariant fails and reports the exact blockers.
